              "text": "کیفیت (keyfiyat) — \"quality\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کیفیت (keyfiyat) غذای هتل پایین بود. Keyfiyat-e ghazâ-ye hotel pâyin bud. The quality of the hotel's food was poor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Bâ keyfiyat — of good quality."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "keyfiyat was borrowed from Arabic and is usually traced to Arabic kayfiyya 'the how of a thing, its manner', built on kayfa 'how', which EtymDB lists."
            }
          ]
        },
