              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تشکر کردن (tashakkor kardan) — \"to thank\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "از راننده تاکسی تشکر کردیم و پیاده شدیم. Az rânande-ye tâksi tashakkor kardim va piyâde shodim. We thanked the taxi driver and got out."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The person thanked takes az. Everyday thanks is mamnun or merci."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tashakkor kardan is built from tashakkor 'thanks', borrowed from Arabic tašakkur (EtymDB), and kardan 'to do', inherited from Middle Persian kardan (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
